[step] The groove roof and the pocket ceiling walk — two stated 45° datums 0.495 mm apart on the normal: the roof rises one-for-one off the seated stop at fz1 + half (z=9.7 and z=146.3), and the column pocket's ceiling walk rises one-for-one off the room top one insertion slip over the flange (z=10.4 and z=147.0). The 0.7 mm between the two figures is the slip over the groove's own opening, read across parallel planes as 0.7/√2.
