[ceiling] The front Z-slide heads' square catches — each bottom rail overlaps the top's full-section foot by 5.00 mm and keeps 0.15 mm of running air, so its flat underside stands at z=160.00 + 8.70 + 0.15 = 168.85. Lifting the seated top lands its flat foot on this face along the whole rail, holding the screwless bottom-to-top seam against lift with full-face bearing. The arm already returns to the wall on its 45-degree under-flare; pitching this bearing face would turn the catch into a cam and give up the joint's square-catch contract.
