[ceiling] The lower Y-seam socket collars' square crowns — each collar keeps complete structural stock over the plug's square slide slot and blind heat-set pocket, so the pin registers and the screw bears on a full section. These two faces are deliberately flat bearing crowns around the cross-pins; changing them into pitched roofs would erase the slot's square pass envelope. They require removable bed-rooted support, and the production-profile audit reads both bed-rooted at 28.20 mm of build-up (`enclosure-front-bottom.support-audit.json`).
